+# The Daily Grind
+
+Run the static application with `pnpm start`. Run automated integration tests with `pnpm test` (Node.js 18+). No build or runtime dependencies are required.
+
+The homepage exposes three WebMCP tools:
+
+| Tool | Input | Result |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `get_seasonal_favorites` | `{}` or `{ "query": "oat" }` | Featured coffee IDs, names, descriptions, detail URLs, and destination identifiers. |
+| `get_site_links` | `{}` | Existing site links with destination identifiers, labels, and URLs. |
+| `navigate_site` | `{ "destination": "cold-brew" }` | Navigates to the same URL as the corresponding visible link. |
+
+Tools read the current page DOM so their results match the displayed content. Navigation only accepts explicitly marked same-origin links. Logout is excluded. The underlying application contains only a static homepage: exposing its existing links does not implement destination pages, ordering, authentication, or rewards.
+
+Registration follows the [WebMCP draft](https://webmachinelearning.github.io/webmcp/) using `document.modelContext.registerTool`, with a fallback to `navigator.modelContext` for early implementations. A browser with WebMCP support and a secure context (HTTPS or localhost) is required for agent discovery. Browsers without the API keep the normal page experience; no replacement API is installed. Tools are removed on page exit and restored when returning through the back/forward cache.
+
+Tests exercise registration and tool execution against a lightweight DOM fixture derived from the homepage, including input validation, navigation restrictions, unsupported browsers, registration errors, and lifecycle cleanup. They do not verify a browser's native WebMCP implementation.
